 yield: implications for optimal colonoscopy withdrawal time</article-title><source>Aliment Pharmacol Ther</source><year>2006</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>965</fpage><lpage>971</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16948808</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B27"><label>27</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morini</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hassan</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Zullo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Detection of colonic polyps according to insertion/withdrawal phases of colonoscopy</article-title><source>Int J Colorectal Dis</source><year>2009</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>527</fpage><lpage>530</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19194715</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Number of Polyps and Adenomas Detected During the First and Second Colonoscopic Examinations</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="gnl-6-64-i001"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>The Number and Percentage of Missed Polyps and Adenomas Based on Location</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="gnl-6-64-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Data are presented as number (%).</p><p>AC, ascending colon; TC, transverse colon; DC, descending colon.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>The Miss Rates for Adenomas Based on the Number of Adenomas Detected During the First Examination</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="gnl-6-64-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>E/G/M, excellent/good/moderate in quality of bowel preparation.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>The Univariate Logistic Regression Analysis of the Independent Variables Associated with Missed Polyps</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="gnl-6-64-i004"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>OR, odds ratio; CI, confidence interval; BMI, body mass index.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T5" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>The Multiple Logistic Regression Analysis of the Independent Variables Associated with Missed Polyps</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="gnl-6-64-i005"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>OR, odds ratio; CI, confidence interval.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>